WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.067
-Thank you for being here, pal.

00:00:02.067 --> 00:00:03.434
-Thanks for having me here, man.

00:00:03.434 --> 00:00:04.801
-You were very nice and
performed on our show before,

00:00:04.801 --> 00:00:06.200
which we loved,
but now I get to actually

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:08.033
talk to you, which is fun.

00:00:08.033 --> 00:00:09.100
-Sick.
-Yeah, this is sick, right?

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:10.634
-Yeah, that's sick.

00:00:10.634 --> 00:00:13.567
-But I'm happy I get to talk to
you and people get to know you.

00:00:13.567 --> 00:00:16.868
And I want to recap your year,
if you don't mind.

00:00:16.868 --> 00:00:18.501
First of all, you're starring on
the biggest show on TV,

00:00:18.501 --> 00:00:19.567
"Euphoria."

00:00:19.567 --> 00:00:21.033
Congratulations.
-Thank you. Thank you.

00:00:21.033 --> 00:00:22.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:22.334 --> 00:00:26.567
-Season 2, the ratings are up
like 1,000% from --

00:00:26.567 --> 00:00:27.767
But I'm just saying --
From Season 1.

00:00:27.767 --> 00:00:30.501
I'm just saying,
there's a reason why.

00:00:30.501 --> 00:00:33.000
-Oh, oh, me?
-Yeah, you're the reason, yeah.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:35.734
And then you're nominated
for your first Grammy Award.

00:00:35.734 --> 00:00:36.601
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:36.601 --> 00:00:38.434
-Not too shabby.
-Sick daddy.

00:00:38.434 --> 00:00:39.901
-Yeah, not bad.
-Yeah, I'm psyched.

00:00:39.901 --> 00:00:41.334
-And then, you know what
I've got to say?

00:00:41.334 --> 00:00:44.234
The coolest thing --
It has to be the coolest thing.

00:00:44.234 --> 00:00:45.667
Paul McCartney is, you know,
one of my favorites,

00:00:45.667 --> 00:00:46.801
one of my idols.

00:00:46.801 --> 00:00:49.100
I love that --
Millions of people do.

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:51.534
"McCartney III" came out.
Great album.

00:00:51.534 --> 00:00:52.701
Then he's a genius.

00:00:52.701 --> 00:00:54.334
He's like, "I'm going to put out
the new album,

00:00:54.334 --> 00:00:56.167
call it
'McCartney III Imagined,'"

00:00:56.167 --> 00:00:59.000
with his hand-picked,
favorite new artists --

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:01.601
favorite artists, and they
just do one of his new songs.

00:01:01.601 --> 00:01:03.801
And you crushed it, by the way.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:03.801 --> 00:01:05.133
You hit a homer.
-Thank you.

00:01:05.133 --> 00:01:07.067
Dude...
-Thank you.

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:08.901
-You crushed it.
-Thank you.

00:01:08.901 --> 00:01:12.033
-What was that like getting the
phone call from Paul McCartney

00:01:12.033 --> 00:01:13.667
asking you to be on his album?

00:01:13.667 --> 00:01:16.300
-I mean, naturally, like, when
you get a call from anything

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:18.634
that you think is spam, you
block the number, you delete it.

00:01:18.634 --> 00:01:19.734
You know what I mean?

00:01:19.734 --> 00:01:21.234
-You blocked
Paul McCartney's number?

00:01:21.234 --> 00:01:23.601
-Immediately, yeah.

00:01:23.601 --> 00:01:24.734
-You didn't believe it was real.

00:01:24.734 --> 00:01:25.834
You go, "that's not
Paul McCartney calling."

00:01:25.834 --> 00:01:26.968
-I still don't.

00:01:26.968 --> 00:01:28.100
I don't even know

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:29.834
if what's happening
right now is real.

00:01:29.834 --> 00:01:30.834
-Yeah. You're here.

00:01:30.834 --> 00:01:32.000
You're on
"The Tonight Show," bud.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:33.267
Yeah, we're talking.
-Yeah.

00:01:33.267 --> 00:01:36.300
-Are you a --
But that must have been surreal.

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:38.534
Were you a Beatles fan?
-Huge Beatles fan.

00:01:38.534 --> 00:01:39.901
When I was a kid, actually,

00:01:39.901 --> 00:01:42.234
I got made fun of a lot
for listening to the Beatles.

00:01:42.234 --> 00:01:44.200
-Really?
-I grew up in Florida.

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:47.100
-Okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:48.567
Okay, okay.

00:01:48.567 --> 00:01:51.234
I don't know what -- They don't
like The Beatles in Florida?

00:01:51.234 --> 00:01:53.634
-There's a lot of stuff
they don't like in Florida.

00:01:53.634 --> 00:01:55.033
[ Laughter ]

00:01:55.033 --> 00:01:57.934
-Oh, my goodness.

00:01:57.934 --> 00:01:59.901
But then you said, "Hey, no,

00:01:59.901 --> 00:02:01.067
you guys got to check out
The Beatles.

00:02:01.067 --> 00:02:02.367
They're next level."

00:02:02.367 --> 00:02:03.901
-No, I succumbed to
the pressure.

00:02:03.901 --> 00:02:05.968
I just started
listening to things like

00:02:05.968 --> 00:02:07.467
"Laffy Taffy" and, like, Nelly

00:02:07.467 --> 00:02:10.801
and I got through
high school, man.

00:02:10.801 --> 00:02:13.634
What do you want me to do?
-"Laffy Taffy." Oh, my God.

00:02:13.634 --> 00:02:15.501
But you -- I know you're
working on a studio album.

00:02:15.501 --> 00:02:17.334
Okay? Your second studio
album, okay?

00:02:17.334 --> 00:02:19.667
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:19.667 --> 00:02:23.167
-I know. What can you tell us?
Can you tell us anything?

00:02:23.167 --> 00:02:26.167
-I'm actually right up
the road, in Allaire Studio.

00:02:26.167 --> 00:02:27.901
The studio's the --
It's, like, the --

00:02:27.901 --> 00:02:29.868
Norah Jones recorded her
first couple albums there,

00:02:29.868 --> 00:02:31.868
and Bowie has his stuff
all over there.

00:02:31.868 --> 00:02:33.701
-Wait. Is that by Woodstock?
Is that Upstate --

00:02:33.701 --> 00:02:34.934
-It's right there.
15 minutes away from Woodstock.

00:02:34.934 --> 00:02:37.000
-That's where I grew up.
-Stop it.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:40.167
-No. I grew up -- Yeah, yeah.
You're Florida.

00:02:40.167 --> 00:02:41.901
I'm Saugerties, yeah,
Upstate New York.

00:02:41.901 --> 00:02:42.968
That's me, man.

00:02:42.968 --> 00:02:44.434
I can totally show you where --

00:02:44.434 --> 00:02:45.701
Yeah, I could take you to my
parents's house, if you want to.

00:02:45.701 --> 00:02:47.033
Yeah.
-Really?

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:48.267
-Yeah, you need anything, man,
you can come stay over

00:02:48.267 --> 00:02:49.300
if you want.

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:50.601
Whatever you want, man.
-Anything?

00:02:50.601 --> 00:02:53.067
-You need a place to crash, man,
you just call me, man.

00:02:53.067 --> 00:02:56.267
I'm your guy.
-So, I have your number, right?

00:02:56.267 --> 00:02:58.133
-Yeah, it's under "Spam"
in your --

00:02:58.133 --> 00:03:00.200
[ Laughter ]

00:03:01.367 --> 00:03:05.534
By the way, I heard that
on the finale this weekend,

00:03:05.534 --> 00:03:08.133
there might be a sneak peek of
one of your new songs.

00:03:10.467 --> 00:03:11.801
-Where do you hear stuff
like that?

00:03:11.801 --> 00:03:13.067
-What are you talking about?
I'm Jimmy Fallon, dude.

00:03:13.067 --> 00:03:15.133
I hear everything.
I know everything, man.

00:03:15.133 --> 00:03:16.200
-I mean, yeah.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:18.367
-Well, do you know
anything about it?

00:03:18.367 --> 00:03:19.767
-Um...
[ Laughter ]

00:03:22.367 --> 00:03:24.367
[ Drumroll ]

00:03:26.701 --> 00:03:28.834
No.
-Okay, wow.

00:03:28.834 --> 00:03:30.000
Alright, maybe I made it up.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:33.934
I might have made it up,
but I don't think I did.

00:03:33.934 --> 00:03:35.434
But there's stuff on
the Internet

00:03:35.434 --> 00:03:37.033
saying that there might be
a new song.

00:03:37.033 --> 00:03:39.367
I'm just saying,
that would be cool if there was.

00:03:39.367 --> 00:03:40.901
Speaking of what's on
the Internet,

00:03:40.901 --> 00:03:42.801
there's a lot of fan theories

00:03:42.801 --> 00:03:44.367
about "Euphoria"
and your character.

00:03:44.367 --> 00:03:45.501
-Oh, yeah, yeah.

00:03:45.501 --> 00:03:47.534
-And I was wondering if we could
maybe talk about

00:03:47.534 --> 00:03:50.634
a couple of the theories
and see if you can hint to

00:03:50.634 --> 00:03:51.834
maybe they're true or not.

00:03:51.834 --> 00:03:53.601
-Let's do it.
-You play Elliot on the show.

00:03:53.601 --> 00:03:54.968
-Mm-hmm.

00:03:54.968 --> 00:03:58.601
-One is that Elliot is actually
Nate's estranged brother.

00:03:58.601 --> 00:03:59.667
Could that be true?

00:04:02.834 --> 00:04:05.934
-I mean...
-No.

00:04:05.934 --> 00:04:08.033
-I'm not even going to lie.
I saw this one online.

00:04:08.033 --> 00:04:09.434
And I looked at it for a while,
and there were

00:04:09.434 --> 00:04:11.033
so many things connecting,
and so many people

00:04:11.033 --> 00:04:13.100
were talking about it all
through these Reddit threads.

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:17.467
And at the end of it, I
was like, "Am I Nate's brother?"

00:04:18.267 --> 00:04:20.434
-You're like, "Yeah, maybe.
It could be true.

00:04:20.434 --> 00:04:21.567
Yeah, it might be..."

00:04:21.567 --> 00:04:24.767
-I almost called them up
and asked them, man.

00:04:24.767 --> 00:04:27.100
-Okay. Elliot --
Oh, I love this one.

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:29.267
This one, I actually love.

00:04:29.267 --> 00:04:31.634
Elliot doesn't actually exist.

00:04:31.634 --> 00:04:34.100
He's a figment
of Rue's imagination.

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:36.033
-Oh, my gosh.

00:04:36.033 --> 00:04:37.868
You wish.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:40.634 --> 00:04:41.901
-Will -- Last one.

00:04:41.901 --> 00:04:44.534
Will Tom Holland appear in
the "Euphoria" finale?

00:04:44.534 --> 00:04:45.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:45.701 --> 00:04:48.467
Tell us. Tell us right now!

00:04:48.467 --> 00:04:49.934
Come on, tell us!

00:04:49.934 --> 00:04:52.567
-I knew I was going to
hear Tom's name.

00:04:52.567 --> 00:04:53.868
-Come on.

00:04:53.868 --> 00:04:55.334
Dominic, you can
tell everyone right now,

00:04:55.334 --> 00:04:56.567
is Tom Holland on this weekend?

00:04:56.567 --> 00:04:58.133
-What I can tell you
is that Tom's

00:04:58.133 --> 00:05:02.067
a surprisingly nice guy
for being Spider-Man.

00:05:02.067 --> 00:05:03.934
You know, 'cause you assume,
as Spider-Man,

00:05:03.934 --> 00:05:05.000
you can do whatever you want.

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:07.400
You can walk into
any room and just

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:08.934
point at someone's girlfriend.

00:05:08.934 --> 00:05:11.200
You know what I mean?
Either way...

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:12.534
He doesn't do that.

00:05:12.534 --> 00:05:15.033
He points at his girlfriend and
kisses her on the mouth.

00:05:15.033 --> 00:05:19.334
And it's nice. It's a good --
Yeah, no, I know. Sweet.

00:05:19.334 --> 00:05:22.434
-How's Zendaya?
She's -- How are all the actors?

00:05:22.434 --> 00:05:23.834
I mean, do they --
-They're amazing people.

00:05:23.834 --> 00:05:25.534
You know, you expect actors to
be a little bit --

00:05:25.534 --> 00:05:27.467
They don't tell you as much
about their private lives

00:05:27.467 --> 00:05:29.133
as musicians do.

00:05:29.133 --> 00:05:30.801
-Musicians just get in there
and tell you everything.

00:05:30.801 --> 00:05:32.133
You know everything.
-Well...

00:05:32.133 --> 00:05:33.701
-Open book.
-Well...

00:05:33.701 --> 00:05:35.701
-Yeah, yeah, to a point.
-To a -- Yeah.

00:05:35.701 --> 00:05:39.133
-Yeah, but actors keep it quiet?
-They do. Don't they?

00:05:39.133 --> 00:05:40.734
What do we really know
about you, Jimmy?

00:05:40.734 --> 00:05:42.334
[ Laughter ]

00:05:42.334 --> 00:05:44.234
-I don't know how
to make a sandwich.

00:05:44.234 --> 00:05:46.734
That's one thing we learned.

00:05:46.734 --> 00:05:48.767
But the show is already
renewed for Season 3.

00:05:48.767 --> 00:05:50.634
Do you think we'll
see you back in Season 3?

00:05:50.634 --> 00:05:51.701
-Absolutely, yeah.

00:05:51.701 --> 00:05:53.200
-Yeah, that's what
I'm talking about.

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:54.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:54.667 --> 00:05:57.100
You're going to perform
for us tonight.

00:05:57.100 --> 00:05:59.767
-Yeah.
-First, I want to show a clip.

00:05:59.767 --> 00:06:02.200
Here's Dominic Fike and Zendaya
in "Euphoria."

00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:04.267
Take a look at this.

00:06:04.267 --> 00:06:06.400
-You know what I feel like
nobody in my life understands?

00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:08.067
Is that, like,
drugs are honestly

00:06:08.067 --> 00:06:10.133
the only way I can be myself.

00:06:10.133 --> 00:06:12.501
-I-I don't think that's true.

00:06:12.501 --> 00:06:13.868
-No, it is true.

00:06:13.868 --> 00:06:15.701
Like, when I first met you,

00:06:15.701 --> 00:06:17.901
I would have never had
the balls to just,

00:06:17.901 --> 00:06:20.434
like, come up to you
and talk to you.

00:06:20.434 --> 00:06:21.901
-Why?
-I don't know.

00:06:21.901 --> 00:06:24.634
I'm just, like,
a deeply shy person.

00:06:26.267 --> 00:06:28.334
And, like, with Jules, right?

00:06:28.334 --> 00:06:32.701
Like, when I first met her,
I was just...

00:06:34.601 --> 00:06:36.534
immediately in love.

00:06:38.868 --> 00:06:40.868
-In love?
-Yeah.

00:06:42.367 --> 00:06:45.033
You saying love
kind of sounds small?

00:06:46.033 --> 00:06:49.467
-What's a bigger feeling
than love?

00:06:49.467 --> 00:06:52.734
-Ah! That's how you
do it right there!

00:06:52.734 --> 00:06:55.267
-Yeah, baby. Yeah, baby.
-Dominic Fike, everybody!

00:06:55.267 --> 00:06:58.400
Check out Season 2 finale
of "Euphoria,"

00:06:58.400 --> 00:07:00.467
Sunday night on HBO and HBO Max.

